<title>AUSTRIA: Creditanstalt 96 final group net up.</title>
<headline>Creditanstalt 96 final group net up.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in billions of schillings unless stated)</p>
<p>					    1996     1995</p>
<p> Group net profit		    2.930     2.166</p>
<p> Group pretax profit		 3.399     2.586</p>
<p> Group operating profit	    6.468     6.138</p>
<p> Group operating income	   19.331    17.342</p>
<p> Group operating costs	    12.863    11.203</p>
<p> Total assets			  687.6	 645</p>
<p> EPS (schillings)		     70.3	51.7</p>
<p> Dividend per share		   12	  10</p>
<p>NOTES - Full company name is Creditanstalt-Bankverein.</p>
<p>According to Austrian accounting standards, operating profit is calculated before risk provisions.</p>
<p>Creditanstalt is majority controlled by Bank Austria, which in January acquired two-thirds of the bank's voting shares from the Republic of Austria for 17.2 billion schillings. -- Vienna newsroom, +431 53112 274</p>
